{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "archon key store conformance vectors - the password-protected seed store of ADR 0007 §A, in cli/{rs,go,ts}. The file is a fixed 134-byte layout: header(62) as the AEAD's associated data - magic arck, version, Argon2id parameters, salt, public key - then a 24-byte nonce, then the 32-byte seed sealed under Argon2id + XChaCha20-Poly1305. Oracles: Argon2id from the reference C implementation (validated against OpenSSL 3.2.4 on this parameter shape); XChaCha20-Poly1305 from libsodium (validated against draft-irtf-cfrg-xchacha-03 A.3 verbatim); the container assembled by hand from the layout in docs/keystore.md, then reproduced independently by @noble. Most cases run at cheap Argon2id parameters ON PURPOSE - the header carries m/t/p and a reader must READ them, so a 1 MiB case pins the format exactly as a 64 MiB one does, and three lanes stay fast in CI.",
